    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="1119" n="1109" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg1109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">840.414/5–2945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">San Francisco</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-05-29">May 29,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received May 29—4:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5. Reference arrangements for one copy of negative of German Foreign Office
                    archives. Lord Halifax<anchor n="71" xml:id="d824-f1"/> this morning informed me
                    that our Embassy in London is pressing for another copy for Murphy and asked
                    most urgently that the Embassy be instructed not to press this request but that
                    we continue the agreement that this whole matter would be kept on the strictly
                    confidential and limited basis for the present.<anchor n="72" xml:id="d824-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d824-f1" n="71" xml:id="d824-f1-content">
                <p>British Ambassador and Delegate to United Nations Conference on International
                    Organization at San Francisco.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d824-f2" n="72" xml:id="d824-f2-content">
                <p>In telegram 4344, June 1, 1945, to London, the Embassy was instructed not to
                    request an additional copy of film for Mr. Murphy (840.414/5–2645).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
